## 0. HOW TO USE THIS DOCUMENT

1. Read **§2 (the project in 200 words)** once. That is enough to understand what you are making slides about.
2. For each slide, this doc gives you four things:
   - **PURPOSE** — what the slide must achieve
   - **LAYOUT** — an ASCII sketch of where things go
   - **EXACT COPY** — text you can paste, verbatim (already short, already bullet-form)
   - **VISUAL SPEC** — what to draw, described so a non-expert can draw it
   - **WHY IT MATTERS** — plain meaning, so you can answer questions
3. Do not invent new numbers or claims. Every number allowed on the deck is in **§7**. If it is not in §7, it does not go on the slide.
4. Read **§8 (words to never use)** before writing anything of your own. This is the most dangerous part of the project — wrong wording makes us look like we are claiming something illegal.

