## 7. VERIFIED FACTS & CITATIONS (the only numbers allowed on the deck)

| # | Fact to use | Source | Caution |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | FRA 2006 recognises rights of forest-dwellers occupying land **before 13 Dec 2005** | FRA 2006, Sec 4(3); MoTA FAQ | — |
| 2 | Appeals: Gram Sabha → SDLC → DLC, each within **60 days** | FRA 2006, Sec 6(2), 6(4) | — |
| 3 | **47,901** CFR/CFRR claims rejected nationally | MoTA Monthly Progress Report, Mar 2026 (reported by Down To Earth) | Say **community claims**, not total FRA rejections |
| 4 | Rule 13 (FRA Rules, amended 6 Sep 2012): satellite imagery is **one of several** admissible evidences; **supplementary, may not replace** other evidence; any **two** evidences required | MoTA FAQ / FRA Rules | Never call it decisive |
| 5 | SDLC/DLC **cannot insist** on a particular form of evidence — Rule 12A(11) | FRA Rules | — |
| 6 | Landsat has imaged Earth since **1972** | NASA / USGS | Note ~79 m in the earliest MSS era; 30 m from 1982 |
| 7 | Corona **KH-4B**, ~**1.8 m**, flew **1967–1972** | USGS EROS declassified archive | Not 1960–72 at 1.8 m — earlier Corona cameras were coarser |
| 8 | **LandTrendr / CCDC** detect the *year* of land-cover change on Google Earth Engine | MDPI Remote Sensing 2018; GEE catalog | — |
| 9 | **DAJGUA** — launched 2 Oct 2024, ₹79,156 crore, 17 ministries, special focus on **22 lakh FRA patta holders** | PIB (PRID 2061196) | The PS text says "3 ministries"; the mission spans 17 — quote the PIB figure |

**Do NOT put on the deck (unverified):**
- Any claim that a court reversed an FRA rejection *because of* satellite evidence.
- Any claim that "pre-2005 proof is the most common rejection reason".
- Any absolute "nobody has done this" / "first in India".
- Any accuracy figure presented as already achieved.

> If a teammate wants to use the Gujarat High Court material, they must first produce the **case name, year, and the exact paragraph**. Until then it stays off the deck.

---

## 8. WORDS — NEVER USE / ALWAYS USE

**NEVER (these make us look like we claim legal authority):**
- ❌ "SAAKSHYA proves the claim / proves ownership / proves occupation"
- ❌ "AI decides whether the claim is valid"
- ❌ "automatically approves / rejects claims"
- ❌ "100% accurate", "guaranteed"

**ALWAYS:**
- ✅ "reconstructs historical spatial evidence"
- ✅ "corroborating / supplementary evidence"
- ✅ "supports human, administrative and legal review"
- ✅ "confidence indicates evidence strength, not legal validity"
- ✅ "the officer or Gram Sabha makes the decision"

**The single sentence to memorise:**
> **SAAKSHYA does not adjudicate forest rights. It produces an auditable, confidence-scored evidence bundle for human review.**

---

## 9. GLOSSARY (for whoever is writing the slides)

| Term | Plain meaning |
|---|---|
| **FRA** | Forest Rights Act, 2006 — the law giving forest-dwellers land rights |
| **IFR / CR / CFR** | Individual / Community / Community-Forest-Resource right — the three claim types |
| **Patta** | The land-title document you receive if a claim is approved |
| **Patta holder** | A family whose claim was granted |
| **Gram Sabha** | Village assembly — verifies claims first |
| **SDLC / DLC** | Sub-Divisional / District Level Committee — approval and appeal levels |
| **2005 cutoff** | 13 Dec 2005; occupation must predate this |
| **ST / OTFD** | Scheduled Tribe / Other Traditional Forest Dweller — OTFD must show a much longer (~75 yr) occupation |
| **WebGIS / Atlas** | An interactive map in the browser with switchable data layers |
| **NDVI** | A greenness number computed from satellite images; high = dense vegetation |
| **Breakpoint** | The year the satellite record shows the land changed |
| **LandTrendr / CCDC** | Standard algorithms that find that year in a satellite time-series |
| **Landsat / Sentinel-2 / Corona** | Satellite image archives (1972→ / 2015→ / 1967–72 declassified) |
| **Rule 13** | The FRA rule listing acceptable evidence; satellite imagery is supplementary |
| **DAJGUA** | Dharti Aaba Janjatiya Gram Utkarsh Abhiyan — tribal village development mission |
| **DSS** | Decision Support System — software that recommends, with reasons, for a human to approve |
| **Provenance** | The record of where a piece of evidence came from and how it was processed |

